issue that concerns many american  families one missouri man says he got an  emergency room bill for more than a  thousand dollars even though a doctor  never saw his son we are looking at that  surprising bill as part of our bill of  the month series with kaiser health news  and npr duvall bot says his wife and  toddler waited to see a doctor at the  hospital for more than an hour then they  eventually left without being seen by  any md  and they were shocked when they still  got a more than thousand dollar bill  the hospitals can  charge you  crazy amounts and  this is what i had heard from my friends  deval bod an immigrant from india always  avoided hospitals in america because he  feared large medical bills but when his  two-year-old son burned his hand on the  stove in april bot's wife mancy called  their pediatrician who told them go to  the hospital i was very much worried the  blisters came on his hand so at that  time i was really panicked the hospital  coded it as a level three a moderately  severe problem  nancy says a nurse looked at her son's  vitals looked at his wound and said a  surgeon would look at it more closely  but after waiting more than an hour they  decided to leave without seeing a doctor  it was so annoying and frustrating i was  just thinking that why isn't someone  coming to to take a look at my son if  this  his wound was so severe  their son's hand healed on its own after  a few days and then the hospital bill  arrived one thousand twelve dollars and  bot owed more than 850 after the  insurance adjustments almost all of the  bill was the facility fee something  hospitals can charge for anyone who  walks in and registers even if they  don't get treated i was really  astonished to see like such a crazy bill  when nothing was done  to my son after contacting the hospital  several times to fix the issue his bill  was sent to collections  bot says facility fees don't exist in  india and the concept of them still does  not make sense to him